abstract: >-
  Hetero-EUCLID is a framework for segmentation and constitutive parameter
  identification of heterogeneous hyperelastic materials from full-field
  displacement and boundary-averaged force data, without stress labels.
  Residual forces of a homogenized model are used to segment the domain into
  material regions, and a hierarchical Bayesian spike-and-slab model
  (building on Bayesian-EUCLID) then discovers a sparse, interpretable
  constitutive model for each region.
